post_install() {
    cat << 'MSG'

  😈  Syntropia has been installed!

  Next step: transform this system into Syntropia OS.

      sudo syntropia transform --check    # dry-run — see what will change
      sudo syntropia transform --yes      # apply the branding + audio stack

  The transform:
    • Installs wine-staging, winetricks, yabridge, yabridgectl
    • Configures PipeWire for low-latency audio (quantum=128)
    • Sets up the Syntropia shell prompt and terminal logo
    • Installs the Plymouth triangle boot animation
    • Applies the OS identity, wallpaper, and Plasma menu icon

  Want the Windows app helper (Wine + yabridge VST installer)?

      paru -S syntropia-brews

  Docs: https://github.com/r4-ndm/Project-Syntropia

MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
    # pacman passes the new version as $1 — no %v substitution.
    cat << MSG

  😈  Syntropia upgraded to $1!

  Re-run the transform to apply any updated branding:

      sudo syntropia transform --check
      sudo syntropia transform --yes

MSG
}

pre_remove() {
    cat << 'MSG'

  🗑️  Removing Syntropia.

  Your Wine prefixes, bridged VST3s, and brew manifests in
  ~/.config/syntropia/ and ~/.local/share/syntropia/ are left
  untouched — they live in your home directory.

MSG
}
